  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "Creating Psychological Safety",
      "description": "A good team captain or leader provides an umbrella of protection so their team can operate without fear (Dara na). When you take shelter in good habits and associate with strong, supportive friends, daily anxieties naturally fade away.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "The क्ष → च्छ Consonant Shift: Look closely at रच्छक (Racchaka). The mighty Sanskrit conjunct क्ष (kṣa) is very hard on the tongue. In Awadhi, it either softens to ख (kha) as in लखन (Lakhan for Lakshman), or it softens into the palatal च्छ (ccha) as we see here (रक्षक → रच्छक)."
      ]
    }
  ]
